<title>USA: Natural History Museum, N.Y., $74 mln repriced.</title>
<headline>Natural History Museum, N.Y., $74 mln repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co., Inc. said Wednesday it repriced American Museum of Natural History's $74 million bond deal, lowering the yield in the 2018 maturity to 5.63 percent from 5.65 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>THE TRUST FOR CULTURAL RESOURCES OF THE CITY</p>
<p>RE: $74,210,000*</p>
<p>OF NEW YORK</p>
<p>REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1997A</p>
<p>AMERICAN MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>NOTE PRICE CHANGE IN 2018.</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa / A1	    S&amp;P: AAA / AA-</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 05/15/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 10/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 04/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>04/01/2004		   75M    4.75  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2005		   80M    4.80  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2006		   80M    4.85  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2007		   90M    4.90  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2008		   95M    5.00  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2009		   95M    5.10  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2010		  105M    5.20  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2011		  105M    5.25  %	100.00</p>
<p>04/01/2018		7,235M    5.60  %	  5.63</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 99.625)</p>
<p>04/01/2022	     19,090M    5.65  %	  5.70</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 99.33)</p>
<p>04/01/2027	     47,160M    5.65  %	  5.73</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 98.853)</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 04/01/2007    101.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 04/01/2009</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on June 19, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
